    "Nasdaq's SOX historical endpoint had not yet added Oct. 5 at retrieval time; the official Nasdaq info endpoint showed marketStatus=Closed and Oct. 5 values. CNBC's greater-precision SOX cache gives +0.28%, while Nasdaq's official displayed rounded percentage is +0.27%; the brief value uses Nasdaq's displayed +0.27%.",
    "Cboe SPX and VIX CSVs provide dated daily rows but no publication timestamp; retrieval/server timestamps are preserved instead.",
    "The local Python TLS trust chain rejected TWSE's certificate metadata, so direct JSON retrieval used HTTPS with certificate verification disabled; the official TWSE calendar content was independently readable through the web extractor, and the official-host URLs and server timestamps are preserved."
